WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.112
By the end of this module, you should be comfortable with a small set of important NumPy patterns.

00:00:06.112 --> 00:00:13.971
You should know how to create an array, inspect its data type and shape, and understand how many dimensions it has.

00:00:14.451 --> 00:00:20.273
You should also be able to perform calculations without manually looping through every value,

00:00:20.273 --> 00:00:28.498
select and filter elements, understand rows, columns, and axes, and reshape data when necessary.

00:00:28.498 --> 00:00:34.423
We will also work with missing numerical values, random number generation, descriptive statistics,

00:00:34.423 --> 00:00:38.733
and simple analytical examples.

00:00:38.733 --> 00:00:46.313
If you understand these core patterns, you will have the numerical foundation needed for later work with Pandas and

00:00:46.313 --> 00:00:48.040
machine learning.
